{"type":"click","text":"R\n    \n      Recommended: Canvas 2D Particle System\n      A single <canvas> element behind the title. Pure JavaScript particle engine — no library. Renders 80-150 particles as glowing circles with additive blending. Vortex effect via polar coordinate math (particles orbit a center point with inward drift). Subtle parallax via mouse/gyroscope shifting the vortex center.\n      \n        Pros\n        \n          Zero dependencies — ~200 lines of vanilla JS\n          GPU-accelerated on all browsers via Canvas 2D\n          Easy to tune particle count based on device performance\n          Smallest bundle impact (~3-4KB gzipped)\n          No WebGL context limits or compatibility issues\n        \n        Cons\n        \n          No true 3D depth — simulated via size/opacity/speed layers\n          Additive blending needs compositing tricks for best glow","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1778030457694}
